---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — The Little AI Company"
  description="Why we exist: to help beginners use AI well — and know when to trust it — by making useful things, not chasing hype."
>
  <section class="about">
    <span class="eyebrow">// about</span>
    <h1>We help you use AI well — and know when to trust it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Most AI advice is hype, jargon, or a firehose of tools. Beginners end up stuck in
      chatbot mode — overtrusting confident answers, undertrusting useful drafts, and
      rushing into "agents" before the basics click. The Little AI Company is the
      friendly fix. Our whole approach fits in one line: <b>learn AI by making useful things.</b>
    </p>

    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <ul class="beliefs">
      <li>
        <b>Make useful things first.</b> You learn AI by finishing one real, useful thing —
        not by mastering every trend. Every guide hands you an artifact you'll actually use.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Judgment before automation.</b> AI sounds sure even when it's guessing. Knowing
        <i>when to trust it</i> is the skill almost nobody teaches — so we lead with it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Skills that transfer.</b> We teach the primitives — prompting, judgment,
        workflows, a second brain — not loyalty to one tool. Models change; the thinking lasts.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prompt mode vs. work mode</h2>
    <p class="body">
      Most people only ever ask AI for an answer — that's <b>prompt mode</b>. The bigger
      unlock is <b>work mode</b>: handing a job to a system that can carry state, stop,
      resume, and show its receipts. That's where AI stops being a party trick and starts
      doing real work — and it's what we'll teach you to do, safely and in plain English.
    </p>

    <p class="trustline">
      Model-agnostic. Beginner-first. Built around useful artifacts, not tool hype.
    </p>

    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/start-here">Start Here →</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/guides">Browse the Starter Kit</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 0 40px; }
  .about h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 52px); font-weight: 900; margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .lede { color: var(--muted); font-size: 19px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
  .about h2 { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; margin: 40px 0 14px; }
  .body { font-size: 17px; }
  .beliefs { list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .beliefs li {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 16px;
  }
  .trustline { margin-top: 36px; color: var(--green); font-weight: 600; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
